# Use legacy peer-dependency resolution — for ONE package.
#
# Why: eslint-plugin-react@7.37.5 (the latest release) declares a peer of
# `eslint ^3 || … || ^9.7`, and this package uses eslint 10. The plugin works
# with eslint 10 in practice (`npm run lint` passes), but a strict `npm ci`
# stops on ERESOLVE without this flag.
#
# Checked 2026-10-15 (S6): it is the only conflict. With eslint-plugin-react
# removed, the client resolves cleanly with strict peers; the root and server
# packages already install strictly, so their copies of this file were deleted.
# (Vite is a single major — vite 7 for both `vite build` and vitest — so no
# Vite peer mismatch is hidden here any more.)
#
# Delete this file once eslint-plugin-react ships a release whose peer range
# includes eslint 10 (`npm view eslint-plugin-react peerDependencies`).
legacy-peer-deps=true
